{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373435551,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"id":"prt_1c8fdc07d001mJjQq1bvGgCM2W","messageID":"msg_1c8fdb40b001tUcubT513r3ZtP","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","type":"text","text":"<think>The /tmp/opencode path seems blocked? Actually the pattern for external_directory allows /tmp/opencode/* but the workdir was /tmp/opencode... Hmm, the error says the rule prevents this tool call. Maybe it's because `cd /tmp/opencode` — no, it says action deny for external_directory pattern *. Perhaps the pip download created files outside. Let me just run without the /tmp/opencode workdir.\n\nLet me try running in /workspace instead.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373435518,"end":1794373435547}}}
