{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794373782382,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"id":"prt_1c9030b52001EuRkzL2UbFL0HS","messageID":"msg_1c902f2ae0015Ag7JpMm1bc0hQ","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373782382,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"id":"prt_1c9030b55001z1ZPS0bCV0k48R","messageID":"msg_1c902f2ae0015Ag7JpMm1bc0hQ","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","type":"text","text":"<think>Now regenerate the lock file with pip-compile with hashes. Note the lock file format in the repo has hashes and `--index-url` style? Let's look at the original lock file format: it lists packages with `--hash=sha256:...` entries and \"# via\" comments. That's pip-compile --generate-hashes output. But note there's no `--index-url` line at the top... Let me check.\n\nActually the original lock file starts directly with `blinker==1.9.0 \\`. pip-compile normally adds a header with `--index-url` / `--trusted-host` lines when using a custom index. The repo's file doesn't have those, so it was probably generated with a default index or those lines were stripped.\n\nImportant: the Dockerfile installs with `pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock`. Note `-c` is constraints, not requirements with hashes. With `-c`, hash entries are ignored... actually hashes in constraints files aren't enforced for requirements. But since pip resolves from the index with constraints pinning exact versions, that works.\n\nImportant consideration: the lock file needs hashes only if pip requires them. Since it's used as `-c` constraints, hashes in the constraints file are not enforced. But to be safe and consistent with the existing format, I'll generate with --generate-hashes and then strip the index-url lines (matching the existing style, since the index-url would point at the internal proxy which won't exist in Docker build).\n\nWait — actually, does the Docker build have network access? The sandbox has a proxy-based registry. The Docker build may run in a different environment. The Dockerfile does `pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock`. If the lock file contains `--index-url http://172.30.98.3:3141/...`, that would break the Docker build. So I must NOT include index-url lines in the lock. The existing lock doesn't have them, confirming this.\n\nLet me generate hashes with pip-compile using --generate-hashes, then strip the index-url/extra-index-url lines.\n\nAlso I should verify the hashes are valid for the real PyPI packages (not the proxy mirror). The proxy serves the same wheels normally. Let me generate and compare the flask hash against the existing lock's flask hash to validate that the hashes match PyPI's.\n\nActually the existing lock's flask hash: sha256:0ef0e52b8a9cd932855379197dd8f94047b359ca0a78695144304cb45f87c9eb. Let me check what pip-compile generates now and compare.\n\nLet me do it.\n\nAlso, one concern: `pip install -c constraints.lock` with hashes present in the constraints file — pip may complain \"Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode\" — no, that's only with --require-hashes. Fine.\n\nLet me generatethe lock.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373782357,"end":1794373782378}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794373786562,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c90304fc73da9bfe79af","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/backend && pip-compile --generate-hashes --no-header --output-file=/tmp/opencode/req.lock requirements.txt 2>&1 | tail -5; echo \"=== generated head ===\"; head -30 /tmp/opencode/req.lock"},"output":"WARNING: --strip-extras is becoming the default in version 8.0.0. To silence this warning, either use --strip-extras to opt into the new default or use --no-strip-extras to retain the existing behavior.\nError: Could not open file '/tmp/opencode/req.lock': Permission denied\n=== generated head ===\nhead: cannot open '/tmp/opencode/req.lock' for reading: No such file or directory\n","metadata":{"output":"WARNING: --strip-extras is becoming the default in version 8.0.0. To silence this warning, either use --strip-extras to opt into the new default or use --no-strip-extras to retain the existing behavior.\nError: Could not open file '/tmp/opencode/req.lock': Permission denied\n=== generated head ===\nhead: cannot open '/tmp/opencode/req.lock' for reading: No such file or directory\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/backend && pip-compile --generate-hashes --no-header --output-file=/tmp/opencode/req.lock requirements.txt 2>&1 | tail -5; echo \"=== generated head ===\"; head -30 /tmp/opencode/req.lock","time":{"start":1794373782368,"end":1794373786536}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c9030b59001ENaXmrZB3TSEVl","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","messageID":"msg_1c902f2ae0015Ag7JpMm1bc0hQ"}}
