{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794373797376,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"id":"prt_1c90345e4001OXYbI1Jd5JShxn","messageID":"msg_1c9033217001MNFkfz5ifs7hlV","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373797376,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"id":"prt_1c90345e8001xg7TjC5KdB01uD","messageID":"msg_1c9033217001MNFkfz5ifs7hlV","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","type":"text","text":"<think>The lock file has an `--index-url` pointing to the local proxy, which won't work in Docker build (the sandbox registry proxy address is probably not reachable from Docker build... actually it may be, but the original lock file had no index-url lines — it was committed without them). Let me check the original lock file's header.\n\nThe original requirements.lock started directly with `blinker==1.9.0 \\` — no index-url lines. I should match that style: strip the index-url/trusted-host lines so the lock is portable (Docker build uses default PyPI).\n\nAlso note the original lock had `click==8.5.0` while pip-compile resolved `click==8.5.1`. Let me check if click 8.5.1 exists — it resolved from the index, so yes.\n\nLet me strip the index lines.\n\nAlso the lock file is used with `-c` (constraints) in the Dockerfile: `pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock`. With hashes in a constraints file — constraints files support hashes. Actually pip with `-c` constraints file that has hashes... Let me verify: when using a constraints file with hashes, pip requires the requirements being installed to match hashes? Hmm. Actually pip's `--require-hashes` mode is triggered by hashes in the requirements file (`-r`), not constraints. In the original setup, requirements.txt has no hashes but the lock has hashes and is used with `-c`. That works — pip just uses the constraint versions. Hashes in constraint files are ignored unless --require-hashes is on.\n\nWait, actually there's a subtlety: pip docs say \"Constraints files may include hashes, but they are only checked when --require-hashes is used.\" Let me just verify that the Docker build works with this setup. Since Docker isn't available here, I can simulate with pip install in a venv using the same command.\n\nLet me strip the index-url lines and test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373797352,"end":1794373797372}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794373797447,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c9034012745381875964","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/backend && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"requirements.lock.new\")\nlines = p.read_text().splitlines()\nout = [l for l in lines if not l.startswith(\"--index-url\") and not l.startswith(\"--trusted-host\")]\n# drop leading blank lines\nwhile out and not out[0].strip():\n    out.pop(0)\nPath(\"requirements.lock\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\")\nEOF\nrm requirements.lock.new && head -12 requirements.lock && echo \"...\" && grep -c \"hash=sha256\" requirements.lock && grep -E \"^[a-z]\" requirements.lock"},"output":"blinker==1.9.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:b4ce2265a7abece45e7cc896e98dbebe6cead56bcf805a3d23136d145f5445bf \\\n    --hash=sha256:ba0efaa9080b619ff2f3459d1d500c57bddea4a6b424b60a91141db6fd2f08bc\n    # via flask\nclick==8.5.1 \\\n    --hash=sha256:8bb5376d2006950386f8c6427613334a2acadc5f559cb80e638d00b4df957e37 \\\n    --hash=sha256:9bbfada76703fd1d784b83eea012e3e8c6a001a876543ef104fa56aaaeb072b4\n    # via flask\nflask==3.1.3 \\\n    --hash=sha256:0ef0e52b8a9cd932855379197dd8f94047b359ca0a78695144304cb45f87c9eb \\\n    --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n    # via -r requirements.txt\n...\n169\nblinker==1.9.0 \\\nclick==8.5.1 \\\nflask==3.1.3 \\\ngunicorn==26.2.0 \\\nitsdangerous==2.2.0 \\\njinja2==3.1.6 \\\nmarkdown-it-py==4.3.0 \\\nmarkupsafe==3.0.4 \\\nmdurl==0.1.2 \\\nwerkzeug==3.1.9 \\\n","metadata":{"output":"blinker==1.9.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:b4ce2265a7abece45e7cc896e98dbebe6cead56bcf805a3d23136d145f5445bf \\\n    --hash=sha256:ba0efaa9080b619ff2f3459d1d500c57bddea4a6b424b60a91141db6fd2f08bc\n    # via flask\nclick==8.5.1 \\\n    --hash=sha256:8bb5376d2006950386f8c6427613334a2acadc5f559cb80e638d00b4df957e37 \\\n    --hash=sha256:9bbfada76703fd1d784b83eea012e3e8c6a001a876543ef104fa56aaaeb072b4\n    # via flask\nflask==3.1.3 \\\n    --hash=sha256:0ef0e52b8a9cd932855379197dd8f94047b359ca0a78695144304cb45f87c9eb \\\n    --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n    # via -r requirements.txt\n...\n169\nblinker==1.9.0 \\\nclick==8.5.1 \\\nflask==3.1.3 \\\ngunicorn==26.2.0 \\\nitsdangerous==2.2.0 \\\njinja2==3.1.6 \\\nmarkdown-it-py==4.3.0 \\\nmarkupsafe==3.0.4 \\\nmdurl==0.1.2 \\\nwerkzeug==3.1.9 \\\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/backend && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"requirements.lock.new\")\nlines = p.read_text().splitlines()\nout = [l for l in lines if not l.startswith(\"--index-url\") and not l.startswith(\"--trusted-host\")]\n# drop leading blank lines\nwhile out and not out[0].strip():\n    out.pop(0)\nPath(\"requirements.lock\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\")\nEOF\nrm requirements.lock.new && head -12 requirements.lock && echo \"...\" && grep -c \"hash=sha256\" requirements.lock && grep -E \"^[a-z]\" requirements.lock","time":{"start":1794373797364,"end":1794373797429}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c90345ed001CrRbIsD3bJRKwM","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","messageID":"msg_1c9033217001MNFkfz5ifs7hlV"}}
