{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373817807,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"id":"prt_1c90395b40016T183QJw8lppfC","messageID":"msg_1c90388d4001eWVf0q18D3aZYG","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","type":"text","text":"<think>/tmp/opencode is not writable apparently. Let me create a venv elsewhere... but external dirs are denied. Let me check where I can write. Maybe within workspace but not committed. Let me check .gitignore. Actually I could just install packages with pip --user or into system (PIP_BREAK_SYSTEM_PACKAGES=1 is set).\n\nLet me try installing into system python directly.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373817781,"end":1794373817802}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794373818458,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c903918b70bda1a2f7f0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"pip install -q --no-cache-dir -r /workspace/backend/requirements.txt -c /workspace/backend/requirements.lock 2>&1 | tail -5; python3 -c \"import flask, markdown_it, gunicorn; print('ok', flask.__version__)\""},"output":"ERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, markdown_it, gunicorn; print('ok', flask.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\n","metadata":{"output":"ERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, markdown_it, gunicorn; print('ok', flask.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"pip install -q --no-cache-dir -r /workspace/backend/requirements.txt -c /workspace/backend/requirements.lock 2>&1 | tail -5; python3 -c \"import flask, markdown_it, gunicorn; print('ok', flask.__version__)\"","time":{"start":1794373817792,"end":1794373818439}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c90395b80016PmTuo0DslKehb","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","messageID":"msg_1c90388d4001eWVf0q18D3aZYG"}}
