{"type":"text","timestamp":1794374234509,"sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","part":{"id":"prt_1c909f17a001aymUT0g82zse9H","messageID":"msg_1c909e422001npWtzcfTnQ3apI","sessionID":"ses_e3702db50ffeNnzuAtZolPliQC","type":"text","text":"<think>linkify-it-py 2.2.0 requires uc-micro-py. Let me check what uc-micro-py versions exist. Latest is 2.0.0. Let me check linkify-it-py 2.2.0's requires_dist.\n\nActually, maybe I should just avoid the extra dependency and disable linkify. But linkify is a nice feature for a markdown notes app (auto-linking URLs). However, adding dependencies increases risk. Let me check whether it's worth it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: the spec says \"A Markdown editor with a live rendered preview (the preview uses the API's rendering)\". Linkify isn't required. But it's a nice touch for a notes app. Hmm — but the risk is lock file complexity and the Docker build.\n\nLet me check linkify-it-py 2.2.0 requires_dist to decide.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794374234490,"end":1794374234504}}}
